  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Kaempferol 3-O-D-Galactoside and SMMC-7721 through a series of molecular interactions. The compound is identified as a target of the 26S proteasome non-ATPase regulatory subunit 14, which is itself a target of multiple compounds, including 2,4-Bis[(4-hydroxyphenyl)methyl]-5-methoxy-3-[2-(3-methoxyphenyl)ethyl]phenol and Javanicoside F. These latter compounds are both linked to SMMC-7721, indicating a possible pathway where Kaempferol 3-O-D-Galactoside may exert its effects through the 26S proteasome pathway, potentially modulating cellular processes in the SMMC-7721 cell line. The scores from the three paths suggest a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, with varying degrees of support from different compounds. The evidence highlights the role of the proteasome in mediating the interaction between the compound and the target cell line, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated.",
